# Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Every real route is prerendered to its own HTML file by `npm run build`,
# and Pages serves an existing static file ahead of any rule below. These
# 301s therefore only catch the unprefixed aliases people type or link to.
#
# The final catch-all is a safety net: if the deploy ever runs a build that
# skips the prerender step, without it every route but / would 404.
/            /en/home        301
/en          /en/home        301
/home        /en/home        301
/services    /en/services    301
/programme   /en/programme   301
/ai-product  /en/ai-product  301
/about       /en/about-us    301
/about-us    /en/about-us    301
/contact     /en/contact-us  301
/contact-us  /en/contact-us  301

/*           /index.html     200
